WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:06.780
At times, Hollywood can seem like one giant,
expensive recycling center, with reboots,

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:10.790
sequels, and remakes galore pumping out of
Tinseltown every other week.

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:15.300
And while many of those projects may be doomed
from the start due to audience disinterest,

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:20.620
bad timing, or poor production, there are
some remakes that have proven to be worthwhile.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.590
Looking ahead at what's coming up, there are
quite a few in-the-works remakes that might

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.199
just work out well.

00:00:26.199 --> 00:00:27.650
Check these out:

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:28.650
Firestarter

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:34.999
Stephen King readers and pyromaniacs, rejoice:
Akiva Goldsman is set to direct a remake of

00:00:34.999 --> 00:00:39.920
Firestarter, the 1984 film starring little
Drew Barrymore, which tells the the story

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:45.589
of a young girl named Charlie who's pyrokinetic
and trying to escape the clutches of an evil

00:00:45.589 --> 00:00:46.589
government entity.

00:00:46.589 --> 00:00:49.499
"Please don't make me DO anything."

00:00:49.499 --> 00:00:53.459
Yes, it was totally a primer for Netflix's
Stranger Things, which is probably why it's

00:00:53.459 --> 00:00:57.929
the perfect time to revive this explosive
entry in the King collection.

00:00:57.929 --> 00:01:02.719
Goldsman has some wide experience dealing
with drama and action, writing the scripts

00:01:02.719 --> 00:01:07.510
for a variety of films like A Beautiful Mind,
I, Robot and The Dark Tower.

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:12.000
So, his screenplay skills will definitely
benefit the project, as he's partnering with

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.600
Scott Teems to co-write the script before
taking the helm on the new Firestarter.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:21.390
No word yet on who'll play Charlie, but the
role will definitely present some up-and-coming

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:26.340
actress with an incredible opportunity to
showcase her star potential... and light the

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.920
silver screen on fire.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.110
Papillon

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:35.030
As the undisputed King of Cool, Steve McQueen
is a mighty hard act to follow.

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:38.310
But that's not going to stop Charlie Hunnam
from giving it a shot.

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:43.830
The Sons of Anarchy actor is starring in a
remake of Papillon, the 1973 film based on

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:46.200
the memoirs of Henri Charriere.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:50.980
A French criminal convicted of murder, Charriere
escaped from Devil's Island before writing

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:52.340
his best-selling book.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:53.610
"I'm innocent!

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.780
I didn't kill that pimp."

00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:01.710
This time, Hunnam will sport the titular tattoo,
but he'll need a little help escaping from

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.229
his South American prison.

00:02:03.229 --> 00:02:08.159
In the original film, McQueen's character
was assisted by counterfeiter Louis Dega,

00:02:08.159 --> 00:02:09.539
played by Dustin Hoffman.

00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:14.530
In the remake, Rami Malek of Mr. Robot fame
will be taking on the role, and Michael Noer

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:15.719
will direct.

00:02:15.719 --> 00:02:17.860
El Desconocido

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:23.909
Released in 2015, El Desconocido was a Spanish
thriller that feels a whole lot like the Keanu

00:02:23.909 --> 00:02:26.620
Reeves classic Speed.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.540
"WHOA."

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:33.160
The movie follows a banker who's driving his
kids to school one day when he receives a

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:37.930
phone call telling him the car is rigged with
a bomb that'll detonate if he doesn't do as

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:38.930
he's told.

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:43.019
As for the remake, well, if you're going to
cast a guy who's trying to protect his family

00:02:43.019 --> 00:02:47.099
from a terrorist, who would you pick other
than Liam Neeson?

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.320
"The one and only…"

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:50.680
"Liam Neeson!"

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:57.300
The action star will play a Wall Street executive
caught in a game of life or death, and instead

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:02.500
of being titled El Desconocido, the movie
will be known as Retribution.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:05.029
Disorder (aka Maryland)

00:03:05.029 --> 00:03:09.230
Have you ever wondered what would happen if
the director of Logan teamed up with the screenwriter

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:10.969
of Hell or High Water?

00:03:10.969 --> 00:03:16.780
Well, the answer is magic — grim, blood-splattered
magic, coming soon to a theater near you.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:23.360
"That's too big.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:24.360
That's what she said."

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:30.169
James Mangold and screenwriter Taylor Sheridan
have teamed up to remake the French thriller

00:03:30.169 --> 00:03:36.200
Disorder (also known as Maryland), a film
about a retired Special Ops soldier with PTSD

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:39.760
who's hired to protect the wife and kid of
a big-deal businessman.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:45.230
The remake will be set in Spain, and a romantic
subplot will give the new protagonist a different

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:46.230
"affliction."

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:51.090
The protagonist is also described as "a potential
franchise character," which means he must

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:55.379
get out of the first film alive … so, um,
spoiler alert?

00:03:55.379 --> 00:04:00.439
As they say, though, it's not so much about
the destination as it is the journey, especially

00:04:00.439 --> 00:04:03.760
when it comes to remakes like these.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:05.260
Miss Bala

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:11.219
Directed by Gerardo Naranjo, Miss Bala impressed
quite a few critics when it debuted at Cannes.

00:04:11.219 --> 00:04:15.739
Loosely based on a true story, this thriller
follows a Mexican beauty pageant contestant

00:04:15.739 --> 00:04:19.310
who's kidnapped by a drug lord and forced
into becoming part of his gang.

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:24.560
And now, the Spanish-language crime flick
is about to get an English-language adaptation.

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:29.980
Gina Rodriguez of Jane the Virgin is set to
play the lead, with Twilight director Catherine

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:31.370
Hardwicke at the helm.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:36.850
But you should probably expect fewer sparkly
vampires this time around and much more bloodshed.

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:40.970
After all, "bala" is Spanish for "bullet."

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:41.970
Toni Erdmann

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:48.010
In 2016, German audiences were wowed by Toni
Erdmann, a comedy that many considered one

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.540
of the best movies of the year.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:54.880
The nearly three-hour film follows an elderly
music teacher named Winfried who tries to

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:59.380
reunite with his business-minded daughter
by pretending to be Toni Erdmann, a goofy

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:02.200
life coach with a bad wig and buck-teeth.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:06.630
In addition to winning over film critics,
the movie also impressed Jack Nicholson, drawing

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:09.260
the Hollywood legend out of quasi-retirement.

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:13.500
After watching the film, the actor went to
Paramount with the idea for a remake, and

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:17.780
earned the lead in the pic, with Kristin Wiig
playing the daughter.

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:18.780
Widows

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:24.090
One of the best filmmakers working today,
Steve McQueen has directed some truly incredible

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.350
films, like Hunger and 12 Years a Slave.

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:30.630
And now, it looks like the British director
is getting into the remake game.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:35.780
Only instead of adapting a film, he's going
to give us his own take on Widows, a BBC TV

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:39.250
series that first hit the airwaves back in
1983.

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:43.610
The original show features a group of thieves
that are killed in a heist-gone-wrong, so

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:46.430
their wives band together to finish the job.

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:51.440
McQueen has had the project on his radar since
at least 2014, but now things are really coming

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:52.440
together.

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:57.130
The director co-wrote the film with Gone Girl
author Gillian Flynn and has since assembled

00:05:57.130 --> 00:06:01.900
an impressive cast list that includes Liam
Neeson, Colin Farrell, Michelle Rodriguez,

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:07.920
Viola Davis, Robert Duvall, Elizabeth Debicki,
Daniel Kaluuya, and Jacki Weaver.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:11.720
The film makes its way to theaters in November,
2018.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.470
Train to Busan

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:18.440
While it slipped past most Americans, Train
to Busan was a major hit in South Korea.

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:22.970
The horror film focuses on a work-obsessed
dad who takes his unhappy daughter to visit

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:23.970
her mom.

00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:27.160
But their trip is interrupted by a swarm of
attacking zombies.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:28.160
Obviously.

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:32.280
As the danger escalates, the central hero
arrives as someone who's only looking out

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:38.020
for himself and his kid but aims to work with
fellow passengers to protect everyone onboard.

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:41.880
Critics fell in love with Train to Busan,
and so did audiences.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:46.230
Like the best zombie movies, the movie blends
monsters with metaphor, and now it's getting

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:49.240
an English-language remake set in the U.S.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:54.050
No word yet on who'll direct or star in the
pic, but if it's even half as exciting as

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:57.070
the original, this one'll be worth the ride.

00:06:57.070 --> 00:06:59.140
Invasion of the Body Snatchers

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:04.050
Based on Jack Finney's classic novel, Invasion
of the Body Snatchers has inspired generations

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:05.050
of movies.

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:10.240
There were several different film adaptations
of the story before the concept of alien body-takeovers

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:14.090
saw its way into other films like Halloween
III and The Faculty.

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:17.540
Now, it looks like the pod people are gearing
up for another attack.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:21.940
Warner Bros. is planning a new Invasion of
the Body Snatchers remake with the help of

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:23.640
producer John Davis.

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:28.610
With its eerie aliens and infectious paranoia,
filmmakers have consistently used the creepy

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:33.800
plot to address all sorts of cultural fears,
from communist witch hunts and 1970s cults

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:34.800
to the military.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:39.170
In these contentious times, it'll be interesting
to see what modern-day topic screenwriter

00:07:39.170 --> 00:07:41.350
David Leslie Johnson will tackle.

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:45.139
There aren't any updates yet on who will star,
but rest assured…

00:07:45.139 --> 00:07:46.700
"They're coming!

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:48.270
They're coming!"

00:07:48.270 --> 00:07:49.310
Thanks for watching!

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:52.040
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:54.240
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

